      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "In a Limited event (usually Booster Draft or Sealed Deck), you can't add basic snow lands to your card pool as you would other basic lands. You can play with basic snow lands only if you open them in your sealed deck or draft them."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "5b2460a5-6ae5-4cad-ba94-1a9e98e6e4c0",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "The Kaldheim set doesn't have any cards with mana costs that include {S}, but some previous sets do. If an effect says such a spell costs {1} less to cast, that reduction doesn't apply to any {S} costs. This is also true for activated abilities that include {S} in their activation costs and effects that reduce those costs."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "975ec9a3-6f20-4177-8211-82526e092538",
      "published_at": "2018-10-05",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If an effect puts this land onto the battlefield tapped, you may pay 2 life, but it still enters tapped."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "975ec9a3-6f20-4177-8211-82526e092538",
      "published_at": "2018-10-05",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Unlike most dual lands, this land has two basic land types. It's not basic, so cards such as District Guide can't find it, but it does have the appropriate land types for effects such as that of Drowned Catacomb (from the Ixalan set)."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "975ec9a3-6f20-4177-8211-82526e092538",
      "published_at": "2025-11-17",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "This land has two basic land types. It's not basic, so cards such as Tend the Sprigs can't find it, but it does have the appropriate land types for effects such as that of Kishla Village (from the Tarkir: Dragonstorm release)."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "975ec9a3-6f20-4177-8211-82526e092538",
      "published_at": "2025-11-17",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If an effect puts this land onto the battlefield tapped, you may pay 2 life, but it still enters tapped."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "8dc067bf-f78f-4ac4-b6e7-b305c42cf0bc",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Although Darksteel Citadel is an artifact, it can't be cast as a spell. Playing it follows the normal rules for playing a land."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If the copied creature has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Clone copies exactly what was printed on the original creature and nothing else (unless that creature is copying something else or is a token; see below). It doesn't copy whether that creature is tapped or untapped, whether it has any counters on it or Auras and Equipment attached to it, or any non-copy effects that have changed its power, toughness, types, color, or so on."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Any enters abilities of the copied creature will trigger when Clone enters. Any \"as [this creature] enters\" or \"[this creature] enters with\" abilities of the chosen creature will also work."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If Clone somehow enters at the same time as another creature, Clone can't become a copy of that creature. You may choose only a creature that's already on the battlefield."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If the copied creature is a token, Clone copies the original characteristics of that token as stated by the effect that created the token."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If the copied creature is copying something else (for example, if the copied creature is an Evil Twin), then Clone enters as whatever that creature copied."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Clone's ability doesn't target the chosen creature."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "42226b87-0746-4ebf-9fd0-108d508462af",
      "published_at": "2025-10-02",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "You can choose not to copy anything. In that case, Clone enters as a 0/0 Shapeshifter creature, and is probably put into the graveyard immediately."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "af32757c-9d3c-4f6c-a6fa-d5729a440382",
      "published_at": "2009-10-01",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "The enchanted land loses its existing land types and any abilities printed on it. It now has the land type Island and has the ability to tap to produce {U}. Spreading Seas doesn't change the enchanted land's name or whether it's legendary, basic, or snow."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "d2d41f12-18d8-473b-9308-3f02d7d791f0",
      "published_at": "2016-06-08",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Humble doesn’t counter abilities that have already triggered or been activated. In particular, casting this spell won’t stop a creature’s ability that says “At the beginning of your upkeep,” “When this creature enters the battlefield,” or similar from triggering."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "d2d41f12-18d8-473b-9308-3f02d7d791f0",
      "published_at": "2016-06-08",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Humble overwrites all previous effects that set the creature’s base power and toughness to specific values. Any power- or toughness-setting effects that start to apply after Humble resolves will overwrite this effect."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "d2d41f12-18d8-473b-9308-3f02d7d791f0",
      "published_at": "2016-06-08",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Effects that modify a creature’s power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Seal of Strength, will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for any counters that change its power and/or toughness and effects that switch its power and toughness."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "d2d41f12-18d8-473b-9308-3f02d7d791f0",
      "published_at": "2016-06-08",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If the affected creature gains an ability after Humble resolves, it will keep that ability."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "8dd5f5af-d2d8-4356-8617-8381081b930c",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Land cards not on the battlefield aren't Forests while Yavimaya is on the battlefield."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "8dd5f5af-d2d8-4356-8617-8381081b930c",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Yavimaya, Cradle of Growth isn't a Forest while it's not on the battlefield."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "8dd5f5af-d2d8-4356-8617-8381081b930c",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Yavimaya's ability causes each land on the battlefield to have the land type Forest. Any land that's a Forest has the ability \"{T}: Add {G}.\" Nothing else changes about those lands, including their names, other subtypes, and whether they're legendary, basic, or snow."
    }
  ]
